{
  "requirement": "Lists the selectable items from a single parse, including the root for the whole file.\n`diagnostic` holds the first syntax error reported during recovery, or `None` for a clean parse.\n`Outline::new` initializes it to `None`.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct Outline {\n    pub items: Vec<OutlineItem>,\n    pub diagnostic: Option<OutlineError>,\n}\n\nimpl Outline {\n    pub fn new(items: Vec<OutlineItem>) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for Outline;\nimpl Debug for Outline;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.outlines.Outline`.\n\n- **Items from a single parse, including the root.**\n  - `tests/outline_content.rs#fn[rust_items_attach_documentation_and_preserve_structural_hashes]` asserts the exact selector list. It starts with the root selector (empty), then `mod[auth]`, and so on. It also asserts the root span covers the whole source and that every item can be selected.\n  - `unknown_extensions_keep_nonblank_lines_and_content_selectors` asserts the root span for plain text and for empty input.\n  - `bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline` covers the other bundled languages.\n- **`diagnostic` is `None` for a clean parse.** The Rust test ends with an assertion that `diagnostic.is_none()`.\n- **`diagnostic` holds the first syntax error.**\n  - `src/outline/tests.rs#fn[reports_recovered_syntax_errors_with_lines]` covers Rust (the error's reported position is asserted) and Python (`diagnostic.is_some()`).\n  - For TOML, the source has two errors. The test asserts the reported position is the earlier one and that the message prefix matches. This checks \"first\" rather than \"last\".\n  - `recovered_outlines_keep_the_diagnostic_and_intact_items` checks that the recovered outline keeps the error (position and \"syntax error\" message) and the intact items. It also checks that `languages::Rust.outline` returns the same diagnostic.\n  - I read the implementation only to see whether first-error selection is shared across languages. `syntax_diagnostic` in `outline/mod.rs` is shared for non-Markdown languages, so the TOML multi-error case exercises the common path. Markdown has its own recording path, but the requirement text does not distinguish it.\n- **`Outline::new` initializes `diagnostic` to `None`.** `outline_constructors_preserve_fields_and_replace_attachments` asserts `outline.diagnostic.is_none()` after `Outline::new(vec![item])`. It also checks the items are preserved.\n- **`Clone` and `Debug`.** The same test formats the outline with `{:?}`, asserts the result is non-empty, clones it, and checks the cloned items' fields.\n- **Struct shape.** `public_exports_match_the_appendix` checks the public inventory against the specification. It also compiles the downstream consumer crate `habeas` against the SDK.\n\nI found no gaps and no acknowledgments.",
